course: dictionary
lesson: 12324
title: Costless and the -less ending
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts. Costless is made of cost and -less. The ending -less means without, so costless means without cost. Other examples are careless (without care) and harmless (without harm).
explain: «The museum entry is costless, so every family can walk in for nothing.» The sentence tells you nothing has to be paid. Costless means costing no money; it is free.
explain: Costless can also be formal. «The mistake was costless: nothing broke and nobody was hurt.» Here it means done without loss, harm or effort. People often say free or at no cost in everyday speech, but costless is a rarer, more formal word that you will meet in maths, economics and exam texts.
fact: Costless means costing no money; free.
fact: The ending -less means without, so costless means without cost.
fact: Costless can also mean done without loss, harm or effort, as in «a costless mistake».
fact: In everyday speech, people usually say free or at no cost instead of costless.
fact: Costless is a rare, slightly formal word, so it is often found in exam texts.
exercise: «The park gate is costless, so every family can walk in.» What does costless mean here? | *Costs no money; it is free | Lost and never found | Locked until the afternoon | Costs a lot of money
exercise: Ben says costless means cheap. What is the closer meaning? | *Free, at no cost | Early in the morning | Cheap, but still needs some money | Expensive
exercise: In costless, what does the ending -less mean? | Very | *Without | Again | Full of
test: «The lesson is costless, so the school does not charge anyone.» What does costless mean? | Expensive and hard to afford | Late, after the bell | Full of cost and worry | *Free, with no money to pay
test: «The mistake was costless: nothing was broken and nobody was hurt.» Which phrase is closest to the meaning here? | Done with great effort | *Done without loss or harm | Done in a hurry | Done twice
exam: «Entry to the museum is almost costless.» What does almost costless mean? | Locked and closed | *Nearly free | Very expensive | Quite heavy to carry
